==English==

===Etymology===
These four notes spell Bach's name; H is used in German musical nomenclature.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|head=[[Bach|BACH]] [[motif]]}}

# {{lb|en|music}} A [[sequence]] of four [[note]]s (B flat, A, C, B natural), included in a piece of [[music]] as a [[homage]] to [[w:Johann Sebastian Bach|Johann Sebastian Bach]].

